IMPORT prelude

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 5), 2002 Revised Edition:
-- Part IV (licensing requirement, regs 19(2) to 22), Part V (station (spectrum) and network (spectrum) licences, regs 23, 24),
-- Part VI Divisions 1 to 3 (station licences and network licences, regs 25 to 58) and Part VII (regs 59 to 64).
-- Text: subjects/sg/telecommunications-radio-communication-regulations-2001/registers/source-bundle/TA1999-RG5.txt.
-- Regulation 19(1) is in sgta-i-rg5-radio.l4.  Amendments to these regulations are in sgta-i-rg5-amendments.l4.
-- Each rule answers whether the licence may be granted, or whether the licensee has done what the regulation requires, from
-- plain facts.  A fee table is data: the figures of Parts I to IV of the First Schedule are in sgta-i-rg5-schedules.l4.

§ `Rg 5 regulations 19(2) to 22: licensing requirement`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:560 | (2) Every application for, and renewal of, a licence shall be made in such form and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:561 | manner as the Authority may determine and shall be supported by such information as the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:562 | Authority may require.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:563 | (3) A licence shall be valid for such period as the Authority may determine unless
-- src:TA1999-RG5:564 | cancelled, suspended or reduced in duration in accordance with the provisions of the Act
-- src:TA1999-RG5:565 | and shall be subject to such conditions, restrictions and limitations as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG5:566 | determine.
@ref Rg 5 reg 19(2) and (3) (src:TA1999-RG5:560-566)
GIVEN `the application is in the form and manner the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is supported by the information the Authority required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 19(2): the application for or renewal of a licence is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the application is in the form and manner the Authority determined` AND `it is supported by the information the Authority required`

GIVEN `the date is within the period the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence was cancelled, suspended or reduced in duration under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 19(3): the licence is valid` MEANS
    `the date is within the period the Authority determined` AND (NOT `the licence was cancelled, suspended or reduced in duration under the Act`)

-- src:TA1999-RG5:569 | 20. A licence, other than a class licence, shall only be granted by the Authority to —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:570 | (a) a citizen of Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:571 | (b) a business registered under the Business Registration Act (Cap. 32);
-- src:TA1999-RG5:572 | (c) a company incorporated under the Companies Act (Cap. 50); or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:573 | (d) such other person as the Authority considers appropriate.
@ref Rg 5 reg 20 (src:TA1999-RG5:569-573)
GIVEN `the licence is a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a business registered under the Business Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company incorporated under the Companies Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority considers the person appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 20: the Authority may grant the licence to the person` MEANS
        `the licence is a class licence`
    OR `the person is a citizen of Singapore`
    OR `the person is a business registered under the Business Registration Act`
    OR `the person is a company incorporated under the Companies Act`
    OR `the Authority considers the person appropriate`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:576 | 21. The grant of any licence referred to in these Regulations does not exempt the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:577 | licensee from obtaining any other approval, permit, licence or other authorisation
-- src:TA1999-RG5:578 | required by law for or in connection with the possession, establishment, installation
-- src:TA1999-RG5:579 | maintenance, provision or operation of any station or network.
@ref Rg 5 reg 21 (src:TA1999-RG5:576-579)
GIVEN `the licensee holds every other approval, permit, licence or authorisation the law requires for the station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 21: the grant of the licence is enough to possess, establish, install, maintain, provide or operate the station or network` MEANS
    `the licensee holds every other approval, permit, licence or authorisation the law requires for the station or network`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:582 | 22. The conditions of any licence imposed under these Regulations shall be in addition
-- src:TA1999-RG5:583 | to and not in derogation of any other condition imposed and specified by the Authority in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:584 | the licence under section 5 of the Act.
@ref Rg 5 reg 22 (src:TA1999-RG5:582-584)
GIVEN `a condition of the licence under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a condition the Authority specified in the licence under section 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 22: the licensee must meet both the Regulations' condition and the section 5 condition` MEANS
    `a condition of the licence under these Regulations` AND `a condition the Authority specified in the licence under section 5 of the Act`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 23 and 24: station (spectrum) licence and network (spectrum) licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:590 | 23. —(1) A station (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum) licence may, upon
-- src:TA1999-RG5:591 | payment of the fees specified in Part I of the First Schedule, be granted by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5:592 | under section 5 of the Act if the Authority is satisfied that the station or network is to be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:593 | operated using a spectrum right granted by the Authority and the station or network —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:594 | (a) meets with and conforms to applicable —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:595 | (i) emission standards; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:596 | (ii) technical requirements,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:597 | as may be imposed by the Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:598 | (b) is of the kind or class that is approved by the Authority for use under a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:599 | spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:600 | (2) Any station (spectrum) licence and network (spectrum) licence referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:601 | paragraph (1) shall specify —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:602 | (a) the conditions of usage of the station or network;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:603 | (b) the duration of the licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:604 | (c) such other conditions as the Authority considers appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:605 | (3) All fees shall be paid in advance and if any fee remains unpaid 7 days after the date
-- src:TA1999-RG5:606 | on which a station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence should have been
-- src:TA1999-RG5:607 | renewed, the following late payment fee shall be charged:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:608 | (a) where the station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence is renewed
-- src:TA1999-RG5:609 | after 7 days but less than 15 days following the expiration of the previous licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:610 | a sum of $10;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:611 | (b) where the station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence is renewed
-- src:TA1999-RG5:612 | after 14 days but less than 31 days following the expiration of the previous
-- src:TA1999-RG5:613 | licence, a sum of $20; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:614 | (c) where the station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence is renewed
-- src:TA1999-RG5:615 | after 30 days following the expiration of the previous licence, a sum of $50.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:617 | Particulars and records of station (spectrum) licences and network (spectrum)
@ref Rg 5 reg 23 (src:TA1999-RG5:590-617)
GIVEN `the fees in Part I of the First Schedule are paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied the station or network is to be operated using a spectrum right it granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it meets applicable emission standards and technical requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is of the kind or class approved for use under a spectrum right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 23(1): the Authority may grant the station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence` MEANS
        `the fees in Part I of the First Schedule are paid`
    AND `the Authority is satisfied the station or network is to be operated using a spectrum right it granted`
    AND `it meets applicable emission standards and technical requirements`
    AND `it is of the kind or class approved for use under a spectrum right`

GIVEN `the licence specifies the conditions of usage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence specifies its duration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 23(2): the licence specifies what the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the licence specifies the conditions of usage` AND `the licence specifies its duration`

GIVEN `days after the date the licence should have been renewed that it is renewed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 23(3): the late payment fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `days after the date the licence should have been renewed that it is renewed` AT MOST 7 THEN JUST 0
           IF `days after the date the licence should have been renewed that it is renewed` AT MOST 14 THEN JUST 10
           IF `days after the date the licence should have been renewed that it is renewed` AT MOST 30 THEN JUST 20
           OTHERWISE JUST 50

-- src:TA1999-RG5:619 | 24. —(1) A station or network under a station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:620 | licence shall not be changed or modified in respect of any of the particulars mentioned in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:621 | the licence, including the radio-communication equipment comprised therein, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:622 | operating radio frequencies and the location at which the station or network is installed,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:623 | except with the prior approval of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:624 | (2) The licensee shall keep an up-to-date record of the radio-communication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG5:625 | comprised in the station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:626 | (3) The record referred to in paragraph (2) shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:627 | (a) contain such information;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:628 | (b) be kept in such form; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:629 | (c) be submitted to the Authority at such intervals,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:630 | as the Authority may, from time to time, require.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:631 | (4) The licensee shall, at all reasonable times, permit an authorised officer to inspect and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:632 | make copies of any entry in the record.
@ref Rg 5 reg 24 (src:TA1999-RG5:619-632)
GIVEN `the Authority gave its prior approval to the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 24(1): the change to the particulars in the licence is permitted` MEANS
    `the Authority gave its prior approval to the change`

GIVEN `the licensee keeps an up-to-date record of the radio-communication equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee submits the record in the form, with the information and at the intervals the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee permits an authorised officer to inspect and copy the record at reasonable times` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 24(2) to (4): the licensee is keeping the record the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the licensee keeps an up-to-date record of the radio-communication equipment`
    AND `the licensee submits the record in the form, with the information and at the intervals the Authority requires`
    AND `the licensee permits an authorised officer to inspect and copy the record at reasonable times`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 25 to 28: station licences and network licences, fees, withdrawal of frequencies`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:642 | 25. —(1) The following network licences and station licences may be granted under
-- src:TA1999-RG5:643 | section 5 of the Act:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:644 | (a) Network Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:645 | (b) Ship Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:646 | (c) Aircraft Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:647 | (d) Amateur Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:648 | (e) Experimental Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:649 | (f) Localised Radio-communication Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:650 | (g) General Radio-communication Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:651 | (h) Satellite Communication Station Licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:652 | (i) Special Purpose Station Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:653 | (2) A station licence or network licence authorises the licensee to operate the specified
-- src:TA1999-RG5:654 | station or network in accordance with the Act, these Regulations and the conditions of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:655 | licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:656 | (3) The Authority must not grant a station licence or network licence that authorises the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:657 | operation of a station or network in any radio frequency band that is within a part of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:658 | radio frequency spectrum that the Authority has determined under regulation 6 (1) to be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:659 | allocated by the grant of spectrum rights unless the Authority is satisfied that the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:660 | circumstances of the particular case justify the granting of the licence.
@ref Rg 5 reg 25 (src:TA1999-RG5:642-660)
GIVEN `type of licence` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 25(1): this is a licence the regulation says may be granted` MEANS
    elem `type of licence` (LIST "Network Licence", "Ship Station Licence", "Aircraft Station Licence", "Amateur Station Licence", "Experimental Station Licence"
                              , "Localised Radio-communication Station Licence", "General Radio-communication Station Licence"
                              , "Satellite Communication Station Licence", "Special Purpose Station Licence")

GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied the circumstances of the particular case justify the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the band is within a part of the spectrum the Authority determined under regulation 6(1) to allocate by spectrum rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 25(3): the Authority may grant the licence for the band` MEANS
    (NOT `the band is within a part of the spectrum the Authority determined under regulation 6(1) to allocate by spectrum rights`)
    OR `the Authority is satisfied the circumstances of the particular case justify the licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:662 | 26. —(1) The licence fees payable for station licences and network licences are
-- src:TA1999-RG5:663 | specified in Part II of the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:664 | (2) The application and processing fees for use of any radio frequency in the course of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:665 | operating or using a station or network under a station licence or network licence are
-- src:TA1999-RG5:666 | specified in Part III of the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:667 | (3) The annual fees payable for use of any radio frequency in the course of operating or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:668 | using a station or network under a station licence or network licence are specified in Part
-- src:TA1999-RG5:669 | IV of the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:670 | (4) The Authority may, in the interest of spectrum economy and after considering the re-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:671 | usability of a radio frequency, the area of coverage involved and the period of use of an
-- src:TA1999-RG5:672 | assigned radio frequency, reduce all or any of the following:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:673 | (a) licence fees payable under paragraph (1);
-- src:TA1999-RG5:674 | (b) application and processing fees payable under paragraph (2); or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:675 | (c) annual fees payable under paragraph (3).
-- src:TA1999-RG5:676 | (5) For any multi-channel radio-communication equipment used for transmitting or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:677 | receiving, the radio frequency fee payable shall be in accordance with the bandwidth of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:678 | frequencies assigned as specified in Part IV of the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:679 | (6) All fees shall be paid in advance and if any fee remains unpaid 7 days after the date
-- src:TA1999-RG5:680 | on which a station licence or network licence should have been renewed, the following
-- src:TA1999-RG5:681 | late payment fee shall be charged:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:682 | (a) where the station licence or network licence is renewed after 7 days but less
-- src:TA1999-RG5:683 | than 15 days following the expiration of the previous licence, a sum of $10;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:684 | (b) where the station licence or network licence is renewed after 14 days but less
-- src:TA1999-RG5:685 | than 31 days following the expiration of the previous licence, a sum of $20; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:686 | (c) where the station licence or network licence is renewed after 30 days
-- src:TA1999-RG5:687 | following the expiration of the previous licence, a sum of $50.
@ref Rg 5 reg 26 (src:TA1999-RG5:662-687)
GIVEN `days after the date the licence should have been renewed that it is renewed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 26(6): the late payment fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `days after the date the licence should have been renewed that it is renewed` AT MOST 7 THEN 0
           IF `days after the date the licence should have been renewed that it is renewed` AT MOST 14 THEN 10
           IF `days after the date the licence should have been renewed that it is renewed` AT MOST 30 THEN 20
           OTHERWISE 50

GIVEN `the Authority has considered spectrum economy, re-usability of the frequency, the area of coverage and the period of use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 26(4): the Authority may reduce the licence fees, the application and processing fees, or the annual fees` MEANS
    `the Authority has considered spectrum economy, re-usability of the frequency, the area of coverage and the period of use`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:690 | 27. The Authority may, in its discretion and without paying compensation and upon
-- src:TA1999-RG5:691 | giving such notice as it considers appropriate, change or withdraw any radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5:692 | allocated to the licensee under the station licence or network licence without assigning
-- src:TA1999-RG5:693 | any reason therefor.
@ref Rg 5 reg 27 (src:TA1999-RG5:690-693)
GIVEN `the frequency is allocated to the licensee under the station licence or network licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 27: the Authority may change or withdraw the frequency without compensation and without giving a reason` MEANS
    `the frequency is allocated to the licensee under the station licence or network licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:701 | 28. —(1) The Authority may grant the following classes of Network Licences:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:702 | (a) Localised Private Network Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:703 | (b) Wide-area Private Network Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:704 | (c) Public Mobile Network Licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:705 | (d) Fixed Wireless Network Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:706 | (2) The grant of a private network licence shall not, unless the Authority otherwise
-- src:TA1999-RG5:707 | determines, authorise the licensee to provide, directly or indirectly, any
-- src:TA1999-RG5:708 | telecommunication service to the general public.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:709 | (3) A Network Licence shall only be granted in respect of a network that meets all
-- src:TA1999-RG5:710 | technical standards and any other requirements which the Authority may, from time to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:711 | time, stipulate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:712 | (4) The Authority may refuse to grant a Localised Private Network Licence or Wide-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:713 | area Private Network Licence if it is satisfied that —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:714 | (a) the licensee failed to meet the minimum channel loading criteria set by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:715 | Authority from time to time for the network; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:716 | (b) the radio-communication service that is, or is intended to be, provided by or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:717 | through the network may be adequately provided by or through a public
-- src:TA1999-RG5:718 | telecommunication system or by any other means.
@ref Rg 5 reg 28 (src:TA1999-RG5:701-718)
GIVEN `class of network licence` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 28(1): this is a class of Network Licence the Authority may grant` MEANS
    elem `class of network licence` (LIST "Localised Private Network Licence", "Wide-area Private Network Licence", "Public Mobile Network Licence", "Fixed Wireless Network Licence")

GIVEN `the Authority otherwise determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 28(2): a private network licence authorises the licensee to provide a telecommunication service to the general public` MEANS
    `the Authority otherwise determined`

GIVEN `the network meets all technical standards and the other requirements the Authority stipulated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 28(3): the Network Licence may be granted` MEANS
    `the network meets all technical standards and the other requirements the Authority stipulated`

GIVEN `the licensee failed to meet the minimum channel loading criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service may be adequately provided by a public telecommunication system or by other means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 28(4): the Authority may refuse a Localised Private Network Licence or Wide-area Private Network Licence` MEANS
    `the licensee failed to meet the minimum channel loading criteria` OR `the service may be adequately provided by a public telecommunication system or by other means`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 29 to 33: Ship Station Licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:723 | 29. —(1) A Ship Station Licence may be granted by the Authority if —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:724 | (a) the ship on which the station is to be carried (referred to in this regulation as
-- src:TA1999-RG5:725 | the ship) has a valid internationally recognised Safety Radio certificate;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:726 | (b) the station is operated by an appropriate number and category of radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5:727 | operators holding a Certificate of Competency granted under the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:728 | Telecommunications (Certificates of Competency for Ship Station Operators)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:729 | Regulations (Rg 1) or a competent foreign authority recognised by the Authority,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:730 | except where the vessel is used solely or principally for pleasure purposes;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:731 | (c) the ship has an accounting authority acceptable to the Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:732 | (d) the ship complies with such other requirements as may be determined by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:733 | Authority from time to time.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:734 | (2) A person who is unable to furnish all the information required by the Authority in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:735 | the application form for a Ship Station Licence may, upon payment of the prescribed fee
-- src:TA1999-RG5:736 | and upon satisfying such other requirements as may be determined by the Authority, be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:737 | granted a Provisional Ship Station Licence which shall be valid for such period and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:738 | subject to such conditions as may be determined by the Authority.
@ref Rg 5 reg 29 (src:TA1999-RG5:723-738)
GIVEN `the ship has a valid internationally recognised Safety Radio certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station is operated by an appropriate number and category of holders of a Certificate of Competency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vessel is used solely or principally for pleasure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship has an accounting authority acceptable to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship complies with the other requirements the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 29(1): the Ship Station Licence may be granted` MEANS
        `the ship has a valid internationally recognised Safety Radio certificate`
    AND (`the station is operated by an appropriate number and category of holders of a Certificate of Competency` OR `the vessel is used solely or principally for pleasure`)
    AND `the ship has an accounting authority acceptable to the Authority`
    AND `the ship complies with the other requirements the Authority determined`

GIVEN `the applicant cannot furnish all the information the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee is paid and the Authority's other requirements are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 29(2): a Provisional Ship Station Licence may be granted` MEANS
    `the applicant cannot furnish all the information the Authority requires` AND `the prescribed fee is paid and the Authority's other requirements are met`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:741 | 30. A Ship Station Licence shall only be granted in respect of a ship, including its
-- src:TA1999-RG5:742 | lifeboats, which is registered or licensed by the competent authority in Singapore.
@ref Rg 5 reg 30 (src:TA1999-RG5:741-742)
GIVEN `the ship, including its lifeboats, is registered or licensed by the competent authority in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 30: a Ship Station Licence may be granted in respect of the ship` MEANS
    `the ship, including its lifeboats, is registered or licensed by the competent authority in Singapore`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:744 | 31. A Ship Station licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:745 | (a) provide on board the ship all documents either considered necessary by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:746 | Authority or required under the Radio Regulations for the efficient operation of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:747 | the station carried on board the ship; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:748 | (b) comply with the working procedures set out in the Radio Regulations and with
-- src:TA1999-RG5:749 | such other requirements as the Authority may determine.
@ref Rg 5 reg 31 (src:TA1999-RG5:744-749)
GIVEN `the licensee provides on board the documents the Authority considers necessary or the Radio Regulations require` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee complies with the working procedures in the Radio Regulations and the Authority's other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 31: the Ship Station licensee is meeting the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee provides on board the documents the Authority considers necessary or the Radio Regulations require` AND `the licensee complies with the working procedures in the Radio Regulations and the Authority's other requirements`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:752 | 32. —(1) A station on board any ship in the waters of Singapore shall be operated in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:753 | such manner as not to impair or interfere with —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:754 | (a) any Armed Forces Communication; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:755 | (b) the efficient and convenient working of any other station or network, or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:756 | telecommunication system or service in Singapore authorised by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5:757 | under the Act or these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:758 | (2) A station on board any ship must not be used if the crew of the ship observes, or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:759 | when the crew has been informed by the Authority, that the working of the station causes
-- src:TA1999-RG5:760 | interference to radio-communication.
@ref Rg 5 reg 32 (src:TA1999-RG5:752-760)
GIVEN `the station impairs or interferes with Armed Forces Communication or any other authorised station, network or telecommunication system or service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the crew observes, or the Authority has informed the crew, that the station causes interference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 32: the station on board the ship in Singapore waters may be used` MEANS
    (NOT `the station impairs or interferes with Armed Forces Communication or any other authorised station, network or telecommunication system or service`)
    AND (NOT `the crew observes, or the Authority has informed the crew, that the station causes interference`)

-- src:TA1999-RG5:763 | 33. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), no station on board a ship shall be used while the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:764 | ship is within the territorial waters of Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:765 | (2) A station on board a ship, whether licensed by the Authority or by a foreign
-- src:TA1999-RG5:766 | competent authority, may be used while the ship is within the territorial waters of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:767 | Singapore for the purposes of —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:768 | (a) safety of navigation, life or property or for any other purposes as may be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:769 | authorised by the Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:770 | (b) communication on such radio frequency bands as may be specifically
-- src:TA1999-RG5:771 | authorised by the Authority, subject to such conditions as may be determined by
-- src:TA1999-RG5:772 | the Authority, where the use of the station does not cause interference to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:773 | working of any other station or network licensed under these Regulations.
@ref Rg 5 reg 33 (src:TA1999-RG5:763-773)
GIVEN `the ship is within the territorial waters of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for safety of navigation, life or property, or another purpose the Authority authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is on a band the Authority specifically authorised, on its conditions, and causes no interference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 33: the station on board the ship may be used` MEANS
    (NOT `the ship is within the territorial waters of Singapore`)
    OR `the use is for safety of navigation, life or property, or another purpose the Authority authorised`
    OR `the use is on a band the Authority specifically authorised, on its conditions, and causes no interference`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 34 to 36: Aircraft Station Licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:778 | 34. An Aircraft Station Licence shall only be granted in respect of a station on a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:779 | commercial or privately-owned aircraft registered in Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:780 | Duty of licensee in respect of equipment, Radio Regulations, etc.
@ref Rg 5 reg 34 (src:TA1999-RG5:778-780)
GIVEN `the station is on a commercial or privately-owned aircraft registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 34: an Aircraft Station Licence may be granted for the station` MEANS
    `the station is on a commercial or privately-owned aircraft registered in Singapore`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:781 | 35. —(1) All equipment comprised in a station on board any aircraft must be approved
-- src:TA1999-RG5:782 | by the Director-General of the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore and a certificate to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:783 | this effect shall accompany the application for the licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:784 | (2) An Aircraft Station licensee shall observe the provisions of the Radio Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG5:785 | and any other local or international rules and regulations applicable to stations on board
-- src:TA1999-RG5:786 | an aircraft.
@ref Rg 5 reg 35 (src:TA1999-RG5:781-786)
GIVEN `all equipment is approved by the Director-General of the Civil Aviation Authority and a certificate accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 35(1): the equipment condition for the licence is met` MEANS
    `all equipment is approved by the Director-General of the Civil Aviation Authority and a certificate accompanies the application`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:789 | 36. No station fitted in an aircraft shall be operated or used while such aircraft is at rest
-- src:TA1999-RG5:790 | on land or on water in Singapore except —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:791 | (a) in exceptional cases or in time of emergency or distress;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:792 | (b) in exceptional circumstances if communication by means of a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:793 | telecommunication line system is not available, for communication in exceptional
-- src:TA1999-RG5:794 | circumstances on matters relating to air navigation and services with the nearest
-- src:TA1999-RG5:795 | aeronautical station, or, if communication with such station is impracticable, with
-- src:TA1999-RG5:796 | any other station;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:797 | (c) for the purpose of carrying out experimental tests with the written approval of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:798 | and subject to such conditions as may be determined by the Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:799 | (d) for the purpose of carrying out functional tests on frequencies other than on
-- src:TA1999-RG5:800 | international distress frequencies to determine the serviceability of the station.
@ref Rg 5 reg 36 (src:TA1999-RG5:789-800)
GIVEN `the aircraft is at rest on land or on water in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in an emergency or distress, in exceptional circumstances for air navigation, for experimental tests approved in writing, or for functional tests off the distress frequencies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 36: the station fitted in the aircraft may be operated or used` MEANS
    (NOT `the aircraft is at rest on land or on water in Singapore`)
    OR `the use is in an emergency or distress, in exceptional circumstances for air navigation, for experimental tests approved in writing, or for functional tests off the distress frequencies`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 37 to 44: Amateur Station Licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:805 | 37. —(1) The Authority may grant the following classes of Amateur Station Licences to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:806 | qualified or approved persons interested in the operation of radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5:807 | equipment solely for pleasure and for the furtherance of radio-communication techniques
-- src:TA1999-RG5:808 | and not for pecuniary gain:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:809 | (a) General Class;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:810 | (b) Restricted Class; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:811 | (c) any other class of licence which the Authority considers appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:812 | (2) Notwithstanding regulation 20, an Amateur Station Licence may only be granted to a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:813 | natural person and shall not authorise the use of radio-communication equipment by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:814 | licensee’s employees.
@ref Rg 5 reg 37 (src:TA1999-RG5:805-814)
GIVEN `the applicant is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 37(2): an Amateur Station Licence may be granted to the applicant` MEANS
    `the applicant is a natural person`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:817 | 38. —(1) An Amateur Station Licence shall not be granted to a person below the age of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:818 | 16 years.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:819 | (2) Any application for an Amateur Station Licence by an applicant below the age of 21
-- src:TA1999-RG5:820 | years shall be countersigned by the applicant’s parent, guardian or by any other person
-- src:TA1999-RG5:821 | approved by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:822 | (3) It is a condition of every Amateur Station Licence that a licensee between the ages
-- src:TA1999-RG5:823 | of 16 and 21 years may only operate or use any Amateur Station if supervised by a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:824 | qualified person approved by the Authority who has agreed to supervise the licensee, and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:825 | that qualified person shall ensure that the licensee observes and complies with all the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:826 | duties and obligations specified in the licence and these Regulations.
@ref Rg 5 reg 38 (src:TA1999-RG5:817-826)
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 38(1): an Amateur Station Licence may be granted at this age` MEANS
    `age in years` AT LEAST 16

GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 38(2): the application must be countersigned by a parent, guardian or other person the Authority approves` MEANS
    `age in years` LESS THAN 21

GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `a qualified person approved by the Authority supervises the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 38(3): the licensee may operate or use the Amateur Station` MEANS
    (`age in years` AT LEAST 21) OR `a qualified person approved by the Authority supervises the licensee`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:829 | 39. —(1) An applicant for an Amateur Station Licence shall, unless exempted by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:830 | Authority —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:831 | (a) have passed the Radio Amateur Examination set by the Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:832 | (b) be in possession of an Amateur Radio Certificate acceptable to the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:833 | (2) The fees payable to sit for the Radio Amateur Examination referred to in paragraph
-- src:TA1999-RG5:834 | (1) are specified in the Second Schedule.
@ref Rg 5 reg 39 (src:TA1999-RG5:829-834)
GIVEN `the applicant passed the Radio Amateur Examination set by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has an Amateur Radio Certificate acceptable to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority exempted the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 39(1): the applicant has the qualification for an Amateur Station Licence` MEANS
    `the applicant passed the Radio Amateur Examination set by the Authority` OR `the applicant has an Amateur Radio Certificate acceptable to the Authority` OR `the Authority exempted the applicant`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:837 | 40. An Amateur Station licensee shall observe the following conditions:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:838 | (a) the station shall only be operated at locations approved by the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:839 | (b) the station shall in all cases be operated by the licensee or by persons named in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:840 | the licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:841 | (c) the station and all equipment used or intended to be used by the licensee shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5:842 | be erected, fixed, placed and used, so as not to cause interference to radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:843 | communications in Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:844 | (d) the licensee shall identify himself by the transmission of the callsign assigned
-- src:TA1999-RG5:845 | to him by the Authority at the beginning and end of each transmission;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:846 | (e) any change in the approved location, equipment, mast or antenna system must
-- src:TA1999-RG5:847 | be approved by the Authority prior to the change being made;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:848 | (f) the licensee shall obtain the approval of all relevant authorities before erecting
-- src:TA1999-RG5:849 | any mast or antenna to be used in connection with the operation of the station; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:850 | (g) the licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:851 | (i) keep a running record of all transmission periods showing the date and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:852 | time of each period of transmission and the radio frequency and type of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:853 | emission employed;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:854 | (ii) preserve the record of each entry made for 12 months; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:855 | (iii) make the record mentioned in sub-paragraph (ii) available for
-- src:TA1999-RG5:856 | inspection at all reasonable times by an authorised officer.
@ref Rg 5 reg 40 (src:TA1999-RG5:837-856)
GIVEN `the station is operated at a location the Authority approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is operated by the licensee or a person named in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it and its equipment are erected, fixed, placed and used so as not to cause interference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee transmits the callsign at the beginning and end of each transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any change in location, equipment, mast or antenna system is approved beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approval of all relevant authorities was obtained before erecting a mast or antenna` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee keeps a running record of transmissions, preserves each entry for 12 months and makes it available to an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 40: the Amateur Station licensee is observing the general conditions` MEANS
        `the station is operated at a location the Authority approved`
    AND `it is operated by the licensee or a person named in the licence`
    AND `it and its equipment are erected, fixed, placed and used so as not to cause interference`
    AND `the licensee transmits the callsign at the beginning and end of each transmission`
    AND `any change in location, equipment, mast or antenna system is approved beforehand`
    AND `the approval of all relevant authorities was obtained before erecting a mast or antenna`
    AND `the licensee keeps a running record of transmissions, preserves each entry for 12 months and makes it available to an authorised officer`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:859 | 41. It is a condition of every Amateur Station Licence that the licensee may not make
-- src:TA1999-RG5:860 | use of encryption devices or equipment in the operation or use of any station.
@ref Rg 5 reg 41 (src:TA1999-RG5:859-860)
GIVEN `the licensee uses encryption devices or equipment in the operation or use of any station` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 41: the use is within the Amateur Station Licence` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee uses encryption devices or equipment in the operation or use of any station`)

-- src:TA1999-RG5:862 | 42. It is a condition of every Amateur Station Licence that —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:863 | (a) messages transmitted through an Amateur Station shall be in plain language
-- src:TA1999-RG5:864 | and shall relate solely to the licensee’s experiments or personal affairs (not being
-- src:TA1999-RG5:865 | business affairs), or to the personal affairs of the person with whom the licensee is
-- src:TA1999-RG5:866 | communicating;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:867 | (b) the Amateur Station shall not be used for transmitting news, advertisements,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:868 | communications of a business or non-experimental character, messages for
-- src:TA1999-RG5:869 | pecuniary reward or messages for or on behalf of a third party;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:870 | (c) except with the written permission of the Authority, no licensee of an Amateur
-- src:TA1999-RG5:871 | Station shall call or transmit to any station other than an Amateur Station;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:872 | (d) messages may only be exchanged with another Amateur Station, except where
-- src:TA1999-RG5:873 | prohibited by law; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:874 | (e) transmission shall not commence without listening in on the radio frequency to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:875 | be used in order to ascertain that no interference is likely to be caused to any other
-- src:TA1999-RG5:876 | station which may be functioning.
@ref Rg 5 reg 42 (src:TA1999-RG5:862-876)
GIVEN `the message is in plain language and relates solely to the licensee's experiments or personal affairs, or those of the person communicated with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station is used for news, advertisements, business or non-experimental communications, messages for reward, or messages for a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee calls or transmits to a station other than an Amateur Station without the Authority's written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee listened on the frequency first to make sure no interference is likely` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 42: the transmission is within the Amateur Station Licence` MEANS
        `the message is in plain language and relates solely to the licensee's experiments or personal affairs, or those of the person communicated with`
    AND (NOT `the station is used for news, advertisements, business or non-experimental communications, messages for reward, or messages for a third party`)
    AND (NOT `the licensee calls or transmits to a station other than an Amateur Station without the Authority's written permission`)
    AND `the licensee listened on the frequency first to make sure no interference is likely`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:879 | 43. It is a condition of every Amateur Station Licence that the licensee shall, if required
-- src:TA1999-RG5:880 | by the Authority by notice in writing, transmit any message provided by the Authority by
-- src:TA1999-RG5:881 | means of his licensed Amateur Station.
@ref Rg 5 reg 43 (src:TA1999-RG5:879-881)
GIVEN `the Authority required the licensee by written notice to transmit a message it provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 43: the licensee must transmit the message` MEANS
    `the Authority required the licensee by written notice to transmit a message it provided`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:884 | 44. The Authority may approve an Amateur Station as a portable or mobile station,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:885 | subject to such conditions as the Authority may impose.
@ref Rg 5 reg 44 (src:TA1999-RG5:884-885)
GIVEN `the Authority approved the Amateur Station as a portable or mobile station` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 44: the station may be used as a portable or mobile station` MEANS
    `the Authority approved the Amateur Station as a portable or mobile station`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 45 to 55: experimental, localised, general, satellite and special purpose licences`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:890 | 45. The Authority may grant an Experimental Station Licence —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:891 | (a) to such educational institutions, training establishments or qualified persons as
-- src:TA1999-RG5:892 | the Authority may determine for the purpose of conducting research and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:893 | development activities, experiments or demonstrations in radio-communication;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:894 | or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:895 | (b) to licensed dealers in, or manufacturers or importers of, radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5:896 | equipment for the purpose of testing, demonstration or conducting research and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:897 | development in radio-communication equipment.
@ref Rg 5 reg 45 (src:TA1999-RG5:890-897)
GIVEN `the applicant is an educational institution, training establishment or qualified person the Authority determined, for research, experiments or demonstrations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a licensed dealer in, or manufacturer or importer of, radio-communication equipment, for testing, demonstration or research` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 45: an Experimental Station Licence may be granted` MEANS
    `the applicant is an educational institution, training establishment or qualified person the Authority determined, for research, experiments or demonstrations`
    OR `the applicant is a licensed dealer in, or manufacturer or importer of, radio-communication equipment, for testing, demonstration or research`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:900 | 46. The Authority may limit the maximum power of a station in respect of which an
-- src:TA1999-RG5:901 | Experimental Station Licence has been granted, having regard to the purpose for which
-- src:TA1999-RG5:902 | the station has been authorised and the conditions under which it is to work.
@ref Rg 5 reg 46 (src:TA1999-RG5:900-902)
GIVEN `the Authority has regard to the purpose of the station and the conditions under which it is to work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 46: the Authority may limit the maximum power of the Experimental Station` MEANS
    `the Authority has regard to the purpose of the station and the conditions under which it is to work`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:906 | 47. The Authority may grant a Localised Radio-communication Station Licence to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:907 | approved applicants to use the following equipment:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:908 | (a) remote control devices;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:909 | (b) local area paging devices;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:910 | (c) wireless microphones;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:911 | (d) transceivers (CB Walkie Talkies);
-- src:TA1999-RG5:912 | (e) telemetry or alarm systems or both;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:913 | (f) wireless data or voice systems;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:914 | (g) cordless telephones; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:915 | (h) any other radio-communication equipment as may be authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:916 | Authority, from time to time.
@ref Rg 5 reg 47 (src:TA1999-RG5:906-916)
GIVEN `equipment` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 47: this is equipment for which a Localised Radio-communication Station Licence may be granted` MEANS
    elem equipment (LIST "remote control devices", "local area paging devices", "wireless microphones", "transceivers (CB Walkie Talkies)", "telemetry or alarm systems or both"
                       , "wireless data or voice systems", "cordless telephones", "any other radio-communication equipment the Authority authorised")

-- src:TA1999-RG5:919 | 48. —(1) The radio frequencies allocated to any Localised Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5:920 | Station may be shared by other users and the Authority shall not be responsible or liable
-- src:TA1999-RG5:921 | for any interference arising from such use.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:922 | (2) Licensees operating on shared radio frequencies shall accept any interference that
-- src:TA1999-RG5:923 | may result from the legitimate operation of stations, including the operation of industrial,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:924 | scientific and medical (I.S.M.) equipment, functioning in the I.S.M. Band.
@ref Rg 5 reg 48 (src:TA1999-RG5:919-924)
GIVEN `the interference arises from other users sharing the radio frequencies, or from the legitimate operation of stations, including industrial, scientific and medical equipment in the I.S.M. Band` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 48: the licensee must accept the interference, and the Authority is not responsible or liable for it` MEANS
    `the interference arises from other users sharing the radio frequencies, or from the legitimate operation of stations, including industrial, scientific and medical equipment in the I.S.M. Band`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:929 | 49. The Authority may grant a General Radio-communication Station Licence to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:930 | approved applicants for the purpose of enabling them to transmit, receive or transmit and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:931 | receive messages by means of radio-communication.
@ref Rg 5 reg 49 (src:TA1999-RG5:929-931)
GIVEN `the applicant is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to transmit, receive or transmit and receive messages by radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 49: a General Radio-communication Station Licence may be granted` MEANS
    `the applicant is approved` AND `the purpose is to transmit, receive or transmit and receive messages by radio-communication`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:934 | 50. It is a condition of every General Radio-communication Station Licence that the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:935 | licensee shall, if required by the Authority in the interest of radio frequency spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5:936 | economy or for any other reason, work with a common base station operated or licensed
-- src:TA1999-RG5:937 | by the Authority or to share a radio frequency with other stations, subject to any
-- src:TA1999-RG5:938 | condition which the Authority may impose.
@ref Rg 5 reg 50 (src:TA1999-RG5:934-938)
GIVEN `the Authority required the licensee, for spectrum economy or any other reason, to work with a common base station or share a radio frequency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 50: the licensee must work with the common base station or share the frequency` MEANS
    `the Authority required the licensee, for spectrum economy or any other reason, to work with a common base station or share a radio frequency`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:940 | 51. The Authority may grant a General Radio-communication Station Licence to an
-- src:TA1999-RG5:941 | approved applicant for the purpose of navigating or detecting objects by means of radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:942 | communication.
@ref Rg 5 reg 51 (src:TA1999-RG5:940-942)
GIVEN `the applicant is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is navigating or detecting objects by radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 51: a General Radio-communication Station Licence may be granted` MEANS
    `the applicant is approved` AND `the purpose is navigating or detecting objects by radio-communication`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:947 | 52. The Authority may grant the following classes of Satellite Communication Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:948 | Licences to enable the licensee to transmit, receive or transmit and receive messages by
-- src:TA1999-RG5:949 | means of satellite communication for such purposes as may be authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:950 | Authority:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:951 | (a) Very Small Aperture Terminal (VSAT) Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:952 | (b) Tracking, Telemetry and Command (TT&C) Earth Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:953 | (c) Earth Station Licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:954 | (d) Portable Satellite Communication Terminal Licence.
@ref Rg 5 reg 52 (src:TA1999-RG5:947-954)
GIVEN `class of licence` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 52: this is a class of Satellite Communication Station Licence the Authority may grant` MEANS
    elem `class of licence` (LIST "Very Small Aperture Terminal (VSAT) Licence", "Tracking, Telemetry and Command (TT&C) Earth Station Licence", "Earth Station Licence", "Portable Satellite Communication Terminal Licence")

-- src:TA1999-RG5:957 | 53. It is a condition of every Satellite Communication Station Licence that the licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG5:959 | (a) must seek the approval of the Authority for access to any space segment and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:960 | shall comply with the relevant rules, regulations and procedures imposed by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:961 | satellite operator for station access, booking and fees;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:962 | (b) may only use or work within the radio frequencies or radio frequency bands
-- src:TA1999-RG5:963 | approved by the Authority for his use; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:964 | (c) must not, without the written approval of the Authority, use any satellite
-- src:TA1999-RG5:965 | communication equipment in respect of which the Satellite Communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5:966 | Station Licence has been issued to provide telecommunication services to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:967 | public.
@ref Rg 5 reg 53 (src:TA1999-RG5:957-967)
GIVEN `the licensee has the Authority's approval for access to any space segment and complies with the satellite operator's rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee uses or works only within the frequencies or bands the Authority approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee uses the equipment to provide telecommunication services to the public without the Authority's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 53: the Satellite Communication Station licensee is observing the conditions` MEANS
        `the licensee has the Authority's approval for access to any space segment and complies with the satellite operator's rules`
    AND `the licensee uses or works only within the frequencies or bands the Authority approved`
    AND (NOT `the licensee uses the equipment to provide telecommunication services to the public without the Authority's written approval`)

-- src:TA1999-RG5:970 | 54. Unless exempted by the Authority, a Satellite Communication Station licensee shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5:971 | at all times comply with the provisions of the International Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG5:972 | Convention and all regulations and recommendations annexed thereto or made thereunder
-- src:TA1999-RG5:973 | as are applicable to Singapore.
@ref Rg 5 reg 54 (src:TA1999-RG5:970-973)
GIVEN `the Authority exempted the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee complies with the International Telecommunication Convention and its regulations and recommendations that apply to Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 54: the Satellite Communication Station licensee is complying as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the Authority exempted the licensee` OR `the licensee complies with the International Telecommunication Convention and its regulations and recommendations that apply to Singapore`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:978 | 55. —(1) The Authority may grant a Special Purpose Station Licence for the installation
-- src:TA1999-RG5:979 | and operation of any special purpose station.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:980 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1), a “special purpose station” is a station not
-- src:TA1999-RG5:981 | otherwise defined in these Regulations that is established exclusively for such purpose
-- src:TA1999-RG5:982 | and upon such conditions as the Authority may specify.
@ref Rg 5 reg 55 (src:TA1999-RG5:978-982)
GIVEN `the station is not otherwise defined in these Regulations and is established exclusively for a purpose and on conditions the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 55: a Special Purpose Station Licence may be granted for the station` MEANS
    `the station is not otherwise defined in these Regulations and is established exclusively for a purpose and on conditions the Authority specified`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 56 to 58: specific provisions for station licences and network licences`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:989 | 56. —(1) The Authority may, in respect of any individual or class of station licence or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:990 | network licence, specify the type of equipment that the licensee is authorised to use and,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:991 | if applicable, the type of equipment to be comprised in the individual or class of station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:992 | or network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:993 | (2) A station or network under a station licence or a network licence shall not be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:994 | changed or modified in respect of any of the particulars mentioned in the station licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5:995 | or network licence, including the radio-communication equipment comprised therein, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:996 | operating radio frequencies and the location at which the station or network is installed,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:997 | except with the prior approval of the Authority.
@ref Rg 5 reg 56 (src:TA1999-RG5:989-997)
GIVEN `the Authority specified the type of equipment for the licence or class of licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is of the specified type` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 56(1): the licensee may use the equipment` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority specified the type of equipment for the licence or class of licence`) OR `the equipment is of the specified type`

GIVEN `the Authority gave its prior approval to the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 56(2): the change to the station or network is permitted` MEANS
    `the Authority gave its prior approval to the change`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1000 | 57. —(1) A licensee of a network shall keep an up-to-date record of the radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1001 | communication equipment comprised in the network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1002 | (2) The record referred to in paragraph (1) shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1003 | (a) contain such information;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1004 | (b) be kept in such form; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1005 | (c) be submitted to the Authority at such intervals,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1006 | as the Authority may, from time to time, require.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1007 | (3) The licensee shall, at all reasonable times, permit an authorised officer to inspect and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1008 | make copies of any entry in the record.
@ref Rg 5 reg 57 (src:TA1999-RG5:1000-1008)
GIVEN `the network licensee keeps an up-to-date record of the equipment, in the form and with the information the Authority requires, submitted at the intervals it requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the network licensee permits an authorised officer to inspect and copy the record at reasonable times` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 57: the network licensee is keeping the record the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the network licensee keeps an up-to-date record of the equipment, in the form and with the information the Authority requires, submitted at the intervals it requires`
    AND `the network licensee permits an authorised officer to inspect and copy the record at reasonable times`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1011 | 58. —(1) Before a station licence or network licence is granted, the applicant shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1012 | satisfy the Authority that the station or network in respect of which the licence is to be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1013 | granted conforms to such technical requirements as may be imposed by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1014 | (2) All equipment comprised in a station licence or network licence shall be approved
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1015 | by the Authority before use.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1016 | (3) Every station or network in respect of which an application for a station licence or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1017 | network licence has been made or for which a station licence or network licence has been
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1018 | granted may at any time be inspected and tested by an authorised officer.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1019 | PART VII
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1020 | PROVISIONS APPLICABLE TO STATION (SPECTRUM) LICENCES,
@ref Rg 5 reg 58 (src:TA1999-RG5:1011-1020)
GIVEN `the applicant satisfied the Authority the station or network conforms to the technical requirements imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all equipment is approved by the Authority before use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 58(1) and (2): the station licence or network licence may be granted and the equipment used` MEANS
    `the applicant satisfied the Authority the station or network conforms to the technical requirements imposed` AND `all equipment is approved by the Authority before use`

GIVEN `an application was made or a licence was granted for the station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 58(3): an authorised officer may inspect and test the station or network at any time` MEANS
    `an application was made or a licence was granted for the station or network`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 59 to 64: provisions for all four kinds of licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1025 | 59. Subject to section 7 of the Act, where the Authority modifies all or any of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1026 | conditions upon which a station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence, station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1027 | licence or network licence is granted or imposes any additional conditions, the licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1028 | shall, at its own expense, comply with the modified or additional conditions.
@ref Rg 5 reg 59 (src:TA1999-RG5:1025-1028)
GIVEN `the Authority modified the conditions or imposed additional conditions, subject to section 7 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 59: the licensee must comply with the modified or additional conditions at its own expense` MEANS
    `the Authority modified the conditions or imposed additional conditions, subject to section 7 of the Act`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1031 | 60. —(1) Except with the approval in writing of the Authority, a licensee shall not —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1032 | (a) assign, transfer, sublet or otherwise dispose of the benefit of any station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1033 | (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence, station licence or network licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1034 | granted under these Regulations; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1035 | (b) permit another person to participate in any of the benefits, powers or authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1036 | granted under such licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1037 | (2) It is a condition of every station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1038 | station licence and network licence that every station and network under the licence must
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1039 | be under the control of the licensee unless the Authority otherwise permits in writing.
@ref Rg 5 reg 60 (src:TA1999-RG5:1031-1039)
GIVEN `the licensee has the Authority's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or disposes of the benefit of the licence, or lets another person share its benefits, powers or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 60(1): the licensee may do it` MEANS
    `the licensee has the Authority's written approval` OR (NOT `the licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or disposes of the benefit of the licence, or lets another person share its benefits, powers or authority`)

GIVEN `the station or network is under the control of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority permitted otherwise in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 60(2): the licence condition on control is met` MEANS
    `the station or network is under the control of the licensee` OR `the Authority permitted otherwise in writing`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1042 | 61. It is a condition of every station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1043 | station licence and network licence that the licensee shall ensure that his employees
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1044 | comply with the provisions of the Act, these Regulations and the conditions of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1045 | licence.
@ref Rg 5 reg 61 (src:TA1999-RG5:1042-1045)
GIVEN `the licensee ensures employees comply with the Act, these Regulations and the licence conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 61: the licence condition on employees is met` MEANS
    `the licensee ensures employees comply with the Act, these Regulations and the licence conditions`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1048 | 62. —(1) Amendments to a station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1049 | station licence or network licence for —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1050 | (a) the transfer of location of a station other than the transfer of a portable or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1051 | mobile station from one site to another; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1052 | (b) any change in the radio-communication equipment comprised in the station,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1053 | may only be made if the station has been satisfactorily inspected by an authorised officer
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1054 | and the Authority has approved the transfer or change.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1055 | (2) Where an authorised officer inspects a station under paragraph (1), the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1056 | may impose a fee of $150 for the inspection.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1057 | (3) Any amendment to a station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence, station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1058 | licence or network licence for a change in the base or repeater station in the network may
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1059 | only be made if —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1060 | (a) the licensee has notified the Authority of the change;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1061 | (b) the base or repeater station has been inspected to the satisfaction of an
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1062 | authorised officer; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1063 | (c) the Authority approves the change.
@ref Rg 5 reg 62 (src:TA1999-RG5:1048-1063)
GIVEN `the amendment is a transfer of location other than of a portable or mobile station from one site to another, or a change in the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorised officer satisfactorily inspected the station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved the transfer or change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 62(1): the amendment may be made` MEANS
    (NOT `the amendment is a transfer of location other than of a portable or mobile station from one site to another, or a change in the equipment`)
    OR (`an authorised officer satisfactorily inspected the station` AND `the Authority approved the transfer or change`)

GIVEN `the licensee notified the Authority of the change in the base or repeater station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorised officer inspected the base or repeater station to the officer's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 62(3): the amendment for the change in the base or repeater station may be made` MEANS
    `the licensee notified the Authority of the change in the base or repeater station`
    AND `an authorised officer inspected the base or repeater station to the officer's satisfaction`
    AND `the Authority approved the change`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1066 | 63. —(1) When a licensee ceases to operate a station or network or when a station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1067 | (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence, station licence or network licence ceases
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1068 | to be valid, the licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1069 | (a) return the licence to the Authority for cancellation; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1070 | (b) if required by the Authority, seal, disable or dismantle the radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1071 | communication equipment comprised in the station or network in the presence of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1072 | any authorised officer.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1073 | (2) Unless authorised by the Authority, the licensee may only dispose of or offer the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1074 | station, network or any radio-communication equipment comprised therein for sale if it
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1075 | has first been sealed, disabled or dismantled.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1076 | (3) Where any radio-communication equipment has been sealed, disabled or dismantled
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1077 | under paragraph (1), no person shall, unless authorised by the Authority, break or tamper
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1078 | with the seal or enable or reassemble the equipment, as the case may be.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1079 | (4) Where a station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence, station licence or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1080 | network licence is returned to the Authority, no compensation shall be paid by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1081 | Authority to the licensee and no fee or part thereof shall, unless provided for in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1082 | licence, be refunded by the Authority to the licensee in respect of the unexpired period of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1083 | such licence.
@ref Rg 5 reg 63 (src:TA1999-RG5:1066-1083)
GIVEN `the licensee ceased to operate the station or network, or the licence ceased to be valid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee returned the licence to the Authority for cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority required the equipment to be sealed, disabled or dismantled in the presence of an authorised officer, and it was` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 63(1): the licensee has done what the regulation requires on ceasing` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee ceased to operate the station or network, or the licence ceased to be valid`)
    OR (`the licensee returned the licence to the Authority for cancellation` AND `the Authority required the equipment to be sealed, disabled or dismantled in the presence of an authorised officer, and it was`)

GIVEN `the Authority authorised the disposal or offer for sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station, network or equipment has first been sealed, disabled or dismantled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 63(2): the licensee may dispose of or offer the station, network or equipment for sale` MEANS
    `the Authority authorised the disposal or offer for sale` OR `the station, network or equipment has first been sealed, disabled or dismantled`

GIVEN `the equipment has been sealed, disabled or dismantled under regulation 63(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority authorised the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 63(3): the person may break or tamper with the seal, or enable or reassemble the equipment` MEANS
    (NOT `the equipment has been sealed, disabled or dismantled under regulation 63(1)`) OR `the Authority authorised the person`

GIVEN `the licence is returned to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence provides for a refund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 63(4): the licensee may claim compensation or a refund of the fee for the unexpired period` MEANS
    `the licence is returned to the Authority` AND `the licence provides for a refund`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1086 | 64. A station (spectrum) licensee, network (spectrum) licensee, station licensee or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1087 | network licensee, as the case may be, shall notify the Authority of any change in its
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1088 | particulars specified in a licence within 14 days of the change.
@ref Rg 5 reg 64 (src:TA1999-RG5:1086-1088)
GIVEN `days after the change in particulars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 64: the licensee notified the Authority within time` MEANS
    `days after the change in particulars` AT MOST 14
